would sing whole concert.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.390
- Oh my God. It's like, that's my thing.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:29.560
I love Chris Stapleton, too.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.000
He's one of my favorite
singers on the planet.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:31.833
And I'm like,

00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:33.990
"How do you have a voice?
Like, your voice is so raspy,"

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.380
but some people are born like,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.273
and some people just
smoke and drink a lot.

00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:38.481
(Joseph laughs)

00:01:38.481 --> 00:01:39.500
But, I think that happens, too.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.520
Okay, so I know we just met,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.550
but I have another request for you

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.110
because I heard that
you speak French with,

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:45.646
I think is so cool and sexy-

00:01:45.646 --> 00:01:46.479
- [Joseph] Oh, really?

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:50.152
- But I want to know what a
French Axl Rose sounds like.

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:51.930
(Joseph laughs)

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.720
- Now Axl Rose in French.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.240
What would he say?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.550
- Something sexy.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.776
- Something sexy.

00:01:57.776 --> 00:02:01.136
(speaks French)

00:02:01.136 --> 00:02:02.568
(Kelly laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:02:02.568 --> 00:02:04.675
- Oh, my God, I love
that you speak French.

00:02:04.675 --> 00:02:06.526
Do you speak any other languages?

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.176
- I mean, I can (speaks Spanish).

00:02:10.308 --> 00:02:12.390
- Okay, like the Latin-based ones? Yeah.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.010
- Well, I mean, I grew up in LA, you know,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.160
but like the high school I
went to more kids, you know,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.754
grew up speaking Spanish
than English, you know?

00:02:18.754 --> 00:02:19.587
- Yeah.

00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:21.680
- So I wish that I spoke
Spanish better, to be honest,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.730
it's always been-

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.640
- I thought that was pretty cool.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.420
- I can, like, I've got my, you know,

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:28.120
my lines in my pocket
that I can, like, say,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.953
you know what I mean?

00:02:28.953 --> 00:02:29.857
I just said like,

00:02:29.857 --> 00:02:32.380
"Oh, I understand better
than I speak in Spanish,"

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.480
so that's, like, my signal.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.430
- That's my thing. Okay.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.820
I impress the owl on Duolingo
'cause I play Duolingo-

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.070
- Duolingo is fun.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.472
- He will shame you, that owl.

00:02:40.472 --> 00:02:42.730
But if you quit doing it for a while,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:44.900
but it's one of those
things I find so impressive

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.520
because when you go, like, overseas,

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.227
everybody speaks so many languages.

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:49.299
- I know, it's true.

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:51.706
- And, like, here, usually,
maybe two, but usually just one.

00:02:51.706 --> 00:02:53.048
I think it's so impressive.

00:02:53.048 --> 00:02:54.910
- I think it changes your mind

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.380
when you speak in another language,

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.760
because your language defines
how you think, you know?

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.180
So when you can speak another language,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.980
it's not just being able
to say the same things.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.150
You, like, you think of things differently

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.080
when you can think in
a different language.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.233
- I love that.

